# Event Horizon rules

- Always keep execution local to the device.
- Use Unix domain sockets instead of insecure or noisy network routes for intra-process messaging.
- Never call `os.system`, `eval`, or `exec` from runtime execution paths.
- Use list-based subprocess calls (`subprocess.run([...], check=True)`) instead of shell strings.
- Treat memory ceilings and thermal conditions as hard runtime constraints.
- Keep the task ledger append-only and auditable.
- Fail closed on untrusted or unsafe code.
- Prune temporary buffers, logs, and transient data after each patch cycle.
